 "text": "Hi! How are you doing these days? It depends on how it makes the recipient feel. If they were babysit it, it's not. If they needed lot of presents, it starts to add up. That's a reasonable move. Don't regift it, though, unless you can taste specifically for who it was meant for in the past. And if you do, offer the gift paper and let them decide who it goes to. That gives the recipient a choice and keeps the gift from getting stuck. Generally regifting something someone else has opened is off limits, as is regiving something with a warranty expiration date just passed. Stick to brand new simple gifts that everyone can use.",
